# Responsive on all devices

Every page and component in this project must work well on phones, tablets, laptops, and desktops.

## Requirements

- Design mobile-first, then enhance for larger breakpoints.
- Test key layouts at roughly `360`, `768`, `1024`, and `1280+` widths.
- Avoid horizontal scroll. Use fluid widths, `clamp()`, flexible grids, and wrapping flex rows.
- Touch targets should stay usable on mobile (about 44px where interactive).
- Navigation must remain usable on small screens (existing hamburger pattern).
- Images, maps, cards, forms, hero sections, and footers must reflow without overlapping or clipping.
- Sticky mobile UI (if used) must not hide primary content; add bottom padding when needed.
- Do not ship desktop-only layouts. If a section looks cramped or sparse on one breakpoint, fix it before finishing.

## When changing pages

Ask: does this still read clearly on a phone and a wide desktop?
If not, adjust spacing, columns, type size, or stacking before considering the work done.